Chapter 8B research completed without scoring. The attempt directory is read-only, so the cumulative manifest could not be updated on disk; a recovery manifest is included below.

The evidence shows a clear and strongly centralized “Fourth Transformation” program, with concrete budgets, flagship infrastructure, social programs, and direct administrative channels. Implementation was substantial, but execution quality was uneven: official audits identified irregularities, incomplete documentation, direct awards, and cost/control problems. The IMF also found that anticorruption implementation, spending efficiency, leakage control, and coordination remained incomplete. citeturn35view3turn35view6turn35view7turn35view8

